  "source": "CCSDS 504.0-B-2 annex G",
  "note": "Attitude Data Messages. The examples are shipped as readable .kvn files under corpus and carried here as decode vectors, hex-encoded because that is the only input form the schema has. Two of the three messages are covered: the APM and the AEM. The ACM of section 5 is not implemented, for the same reason the ODM's OCM is not \u2014 it is roughly three times the size of the other two together, arrived with the 2024 issue, and adoption is thin. What the vectors assert is which blocks a message carried, the frames a rotation goes between, and for an AEM the attitude type and the resulting line width. The numbers are floats, which a vector field cannot hold, and are checked in pkg/adm against the same published text.",
